# `@moriyoshi/drawio-svg-optimizer` is published to GitHub Packages, not to the
# public registry, so the scope has to be pointed at it. Only the mapping lives
# here; no credential does.
#
# GitHub Packages requires a token even to *read* a public package. CI gets one
# from `actions/setup-node` (`registry-url` + `NODE_AUTH_TOKEN`), which writes
# its own npmrc; locally it comes from `~/.npmrc`. Putting
# `//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}` in this file instead
# would make *every* npm command fail ("Failed to replace env in config") on any
# machine where that variable is unset.
@moriyoshi:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
